//! The artifact body encoding: a canonical, self-delimiting byte encoding of every type an encoded
//! `CompiledFunction` or pipeline artifact carries. It needs no `serde`.
//!
//! - Integers are fixed-width little-endian; `bool` is one byte, 0 or 1.
//! - A sequence (vector, string, byte slice, map, set) is a `u32` count, then its items. A count
//!   is checked against the bytes left before anything is reserved, so hostile input cannot
//!   allocate more than its own size.
//! - Maps and sets are written in order and must decode strictly increasing (one encoding per
//!   value).
//! - A struct is its fields in declaration order. An enum is its variant name, then the
//!   variant's fields; names keep the encoding stable when variants are reordered.
//!
//! Every impl is generated by [`codec_struct!`] or [`codec_enum!`], which destructure and match
//! without wildcards: a field or variant added to a type without a line here is a compile error,
//! so the encoding stays total by construction.
//!
//! The same impls give each value's node in a content digest ([`Codec::digest`], `digest`): structs
//! and enum variants by their field and variant names, so a digest survives an added field whose
//! value is zero and reordered or inserted variants.

